<h2>Several code blocks on one slide</h2>

<p>
  Blocks without an <c>#id</c> are independent: each is its own animation, side by side or one below the other.
</p>

<code lang=typescript>
  const a = 1;
</code>

<p>Text can sit between the blocks.</p>

<code lang=python>
  b = 2
</code>

<step>
  <p>Blocks with the same <c>#id</c> are frames of one block. The second click morphs it:</p>
</step>

<step at=1>
  <code lang=typescript>
    <frame>
      function f() { return 1; }
    </frame>
    <frame>
      function f() { return 2; }
    </frame>
  </code>
</step>
